{"verdict":"approved","issues":[{"severity":"minor","file":"src/pages/_app.tsx","line":97,"description":"ContentstackLivePreview.init is called unconditionally with enable: true on every page load, including production sessions outside the CMS preview iframe. The SDK stays dormant without the CMS postMessage handshake, so behavior is safe, but gating init on the live-preview hash params (e.g. live_preview query/hash presence) would avoid unnecessary SDK initialization in production.","suggestedFix":"Wrap ContentstackLivePreview.init in a check for preview-mode indicators (e.g. window.location.hash contains live_preview or contentstack preview params) before initializing."},{"severity":"minor","file":"src/pages/_app.tsx","line":127,"description":"Protected/gated page verification criterion: the preview override in useContent applies whenever onEntryChange fires, with no check of the page's auth/gated state. In practice onEntryChange only fires inside the CMS preview iframe and the story notes protected-page preview 'might not be possible' as a known limitation, so this is acceptable for part 1, but there is no explicit guard preventing preview state from overriding a gated page's content.","suggestedFix":"If protected-page preview must be excluded in a later part, gate setPreviewPage on a flag from pageProps indicating the page is not protected, or clear previewPage when the session/gated state indicates a protected route."},{"severity":"minor","file":"src/context/contentstackContext.tsx","line":22,"description":"Deviation from the plan of record: the plan prescribed adding an updater field to IContentstackContext, but a separate LivePreviewContext was created instead, requiring an edit to useContent.ts (which the plan marked as no-edit). The chosen mechanism is functionally equivalent and addresses the root cause (non-reactive context) cleanly, so this is advisory only — the separate context avoids mutating the server-props-driven ContentstackContext shape.","suggestedFix":"No change required; if aligning strictly with the plan is desired, fold previewPage into IContentstackContext instead of a parallel context."},{"severity":"minor","file":"src/hooks/useContent.ts","line":10,"description":"When previewPage is set, effectiveContent is a new object identity on every render, so the useCallback dependency [effectiveContent] recreates getContentByKey each render during an active preview session. Impact is confined to preview mode (CMS iframe), so this is cosmetic.","suggestedFix":"Memoize with useMemo: const effectiveContent = useMemo(() => previewPage ? { ...content, page: previewPage } : content, [content, previewPage]);"},{"severity":"minor","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":99,"description":"The fallback host 'api.contentstack.io' is a hardcoded URL string duplicated from the SDK's own default. The Stack type requires host, so it cannot simply be omitted, but the literal could drift from the SDK default.","suggestedFix":"Optional: reference the SDK default or document that this literal intentionally mirrors the SDK's default host; not worth a constants file for a single fallback."}],"summary":"Approved. The implementation addresses the prescribed root cause: live_preview config was added to the Stack options in contentstack.ts (verified against the installed contentstack SDK — the LivePreview type genuinely requires the management_token key, and the comment correctly documents that it carries the Live Preview token, not a write-access management token), ContentstackLivePreview is initialized in _app.tsx with an onEntryChange callback that re-fetches via the existing ContentstackFactory.createContentTypeEntryQuery (exported rather than duplicated — correct reuse of the prescribed helper at contentstack.ts:185), and the context layer was made reactive so all useContent consumers re-render. Successive onEntryChange events each re-fetch and setPreviewPage in sequence, satisfying the multi-change criterion; routeChangeComplete resets preview state to prevent cross-page leakage; the empty catch is documented as best-effort. The no-preview path is untouched: when previewPage is undefined, useContent returns the original content object unchanged, so Homepage and Discover Article render published content identically. No literal credentials were introduced — only process.env references (CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN/HOST) and the SDK-default host string, which is correct practice. The main deviation from the plan (separate LivePreviewContext instead of an updater on IContentstackContext, which required a small useContent.ts edit) is functionally equivalent and arguably cleaner, so it is advisory. Test coverage is owned by the test-writer agent and was not assessed."}
